<title>GERMANY: German banks plan to implement sick pay cut.</title>
<headline>German banks plan to implement sick pay cut.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of German Bank employers said on Thursday that banks would implement a cut in sick pay to 80 percent of normal pay, in line with a recent change in labour laws.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the association said that the existing wage agreement for the banking sector stated that sick pay arrangements should be determined by whatever legislation currently applied.</p>
<p>As a result, the cut would come into force for bank workers on October 1 or November 1 at the latest, the spokesman said in response to a Reuter query.</p>
</text>
